8cfd0fec5acfd75c41fb5db704c2a460b57c5657.body:
Let \(P_{\varepsilon}^{\mathrm{wit}}\) be the two-class Bernoulli proxy witness law from \(\cref{obj:def:two-class-witness}\), and let \((P_{\varepsilon}^{\mathrm{wit}})_O\) be its observed-data marginal from \(\cref{obj:def:observed-margin}\). Suppose that
\begin{itemize}
\item \textbf{(Perturbation.)} the collision-witness effect displacement \(\varepsilon\in\mathbb R\) satisfies \(0\le \varepsilon\le 1/8\);
\item \textbf{(Arm.)} \(t\in\{0,1\}\).
\end{itemize}
Then the observed mass of the treatment arm \(t\) is
\[
(P_{\varepsilon}^{\mathrm{wit}})_O(T=t)
=
\begin{cases}
12/25, & t=0,\\
13/25, & t=1.
\end{cases}
\]

96ca1136d174c6073a4b00b3c708465c7394e495.body:
For any real numbers \(g\) and \(h\), assume:
\begin{itemize}
\item \textbf{(Gap range.)} \(0\le g\le 1/4\).
\item \textbf{(Path perturbation.)} \(|h|\le 1/100\).
\end{itemize}
Then the path law \(P_{g,h}\) of \(\cref{obj:def:path-law-family}\) belongs to the uniformly conditioned proxy causal model class \(\mathcal M\) of \(\cref{obj:def:model-class}\) with \(k=d_x=d_z=2\), \(L=2\), \(\pi_0=1/10\), and \(\sigma_0=1/10\). In particular, \(P_{g,h}\) satisfies the core numerical domain for these dimensions and constants, together with \(\cref{obj:ass:reference-proxy-separation,obj:ass:target-proxy-separation,obj:ass:consistency,obj:ass:latent-ignorability,obj:ass:anchor,obj:ass:bounded-x,obj:ass:bounded-proxy-product,obj:ass:bounded-outcome-proxy-product,obj:ass:latent-arm-positivity,obj:ass:proxy-rank-margin}\).

087496821b201dbb8505fb50998ee180faf3430f.body:
Let \(P_{g,h}\) be the factorization-preserving two-class path law of \(\cref{obj:def:path-law-family}\). Suppose that
\begin{itemize}
\item \textbf{(Gap range.)} \(0\le g\le 1/4\).
\item \textbf{(Tangent amplitude.)} \(|h|\le 1/100\).
\end{itemize}
Then \(P_{g,h}\) satisfies the proxy-rank margin in \(\cref{obj:ass:proxy-rank-margin}\) with proxy-rank singular-value margin \(\sigma_0=1/10\): the reference-proxy feature matrices \(A_0\) and \(A_1\) from \(\cref{obj:def:reference-feature}\), and the target-proxy feature matrix \(B\) from \(\cref{obj:def:target-feature}\), all formed from \(P_{g,h}\), have smallest singular value at least \(1/10\).

