15c3f8d240439b6ab147cfc10163e56903c89263.body:
For fixed \(k,d_x,d_z\in\mathbb N\) and \(L,\pi_0,\sigma_0\in\mathbb R\), the uniformly conditioned proxy causal model class \(\mathcal M\) consists of full-data probability laws \(P\) on records \((U,T,X,Z,Y(0),Y(1),Y)\) such that \(U\in\{1,\ldots,k\}\), \(T\in\{0,1\}\), \(X\in\mathbb R^{d_x}\), \(Z\in\mathbb R^{d_z}\), and \(Y(0),Y(1),Y\in\mathbb R\), with:
\begin{itemize}
\item \textbf{(Core parameter domain.)} \(2\le k\), \(k\le d_x\), \(k\le d_z\), \(1\le L\), \(0<\pi_0\le 1/(2k)\), and \(0<\sigma_0\le 1\).
\item \textbf{(Proxy and causal structure.)} \(P\) satisfies \(\cref{obj:ass:reference-proxy-separation,obj:ass:target-proxy-separation,obj:ass:consistency,obj:ass:latent-ignorability,obj:ass:anchor}\).
\item \textbf{(Boundedness and conditioning.)} \(P\) satisfies \(\cref{obj:ass:bounded-x,obj:ass:bounded-proxy-product,obj:ass:bounded-outcome-proxy-product,obj:ass:latent-arm-positivity,obj:ass:proxy-rank-margin}\).
\end{itemize}

af94bba903b0687f8d076f359f332b8c04f497d5.body:
For real numbers \(g\), the local effect-gap scale, and \(h\), suppose that
\begin{itemize}
\item \textbf{(Gap scale.)} \(0<g\le 1/4\).
\item \textbf{(Path displacement.)} \(|h|\le 1/100\).
\end{itemize}
Then the path law \(P_{g,h}\) of \cref{obj:def:path-law-family} belongs to the gap-local stratum \(\mathcal M(g)\) of \cref{obj:def:gap-stratum} with constants \(L=2\), \(\pi_0=1/10\), and \(\sigma_0=1/10\). Equivalently, \(P_{g,h}\) lies in the model class \(\mathcal M\) of \cref{obj:def:model-class} under the boundedness, latent-arm positivity, and proxy-rank conditions in \cref{obj:ass:bounded-x,obj:ass:latent-arm-positivity,obj:ass:proxy-rank-margin}; its smallest positive effect gap \(\delta(P_{g,h})\) from \cref{obj:def:effect-gap} satisfies the gap window in \cref{obj:ass:gap-window},
\[
\frac{g}{2}\le \delta(P_{g,h})\le 2g;
\]
and its latent effects from \cref{obj:def:latent-effect} satisfy the distinctness condition in \cref{obj:ass:distinct-effects}.

